Usage: agent-deck inbox <session-id>
       agent-deck inbox drain [--json] <session-id>
       agent-deck inbox export [--json]
       agent-deck inbox writer-status [--json]
       agent-deck inbox dead-letter <list|show|retry|purge>

Drain pending completion events from the parent's durable outbox.
The `drain` form (issue #1225) preserves distinct turns per child and
dedups re-delivery via turn_fingerprint; run it first on every
heartbeat. Reading clears the inbox.
The `export` form (issue #1948) READS this host's completion and
transition records without consuming anything; it is what a
conductor on another machine runs over ssh via `remote drain`.
The `writer-status` form reports whether a notify-daemon is
actually recording transitions here — without it, an empty export
cannot be told apart from a host where nothing has been watching.
The `dead-letter` family safely inspects, retries, or purges terminal
delivery failures; run `agent-deck inbox dead-letter help` for details.
